  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 10, P = 17. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[12, 0, 9, 6, 15, 13, 0, 16, 12, 14], [2, 16, 9, 11, 12, 4, 4, 11, 4, 3], [10, 14, 12, 10, 0, 13, 8, 6, 5, 3]], sigma = [1, 0, 6, 4, 3, 9, 2, 8, 7, 5], B = [0, 0, 0, 13, 13, 7, 0, 1, 1, 7].",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data"
  ],
  "date": "2026",
  "novelty": "known_parameters",
  "notes": "Literature baseline: a reproduction of a code published with arXiv:2609.30069, rebuilt from the authors' data repository (https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data/blob/306b31d/codes/reverse_fold/j3l10/specs/reverse_j3l10_p17_k36.json). Not a new construction. The authors report d = 6 as exact. Their lower-bound search output is not in the repository, so this entry carries an upper bound backed by their weight-6 Pauli logical, stored as the witness."
